        "title": "Restore Cursor diagnostics and OpenCode workspace parity",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Restore the custom Cursor widget range summaries, calendar dates, conservative exact/approximate cost diagnostics, bounded request details, and one-row scrolling behavior.\n- Restore OpenCode workspace discovery, display-safe workspace accounts, menu switching, stale-response isolation, and widget workspace switching.\n- Preserve backward-compatible widget snapshots, provider data siloing, and credential isolation.\n\n## User-visible changes\n\n- Cursor widgets and menu diagnostics now show the selected Cycle/30d range, date period, bounded recent request details, and truthful exact/approximate/lower-bound local estimates.\n- OpenCode users can discover/save multiple workspaces, switch them from the menu, and switch widget workspace chips without exposing cookies or auth headers.\n- Failed first-time OpenCode discovery no longer persists a credential, and recovery copy is actionable.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Codex plan review: APPROVED (`gpt-5.6-terra`, four plan-review rounds).\n- Codex code review: APPROVED (`gpt-5.6-terra`, three review rounds; no blocking issues).\n- `./Scripts/lint.sh format`: 0/724 files formatted.\n- `pnpm check`: 0/724 files require formatting; 0 lint violations.\n- `swiftlint --strict`: 0 violations.\n- Focused parity suite: 172 tests in 19 suites passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- `CODEXBAR_SIGNING=adhoc ./Scripts/compile_and_run.sh --wait`: completed, generated WidgetKit metadata, packaged/signed the app, and launched successfully.\n- Live process check confirmed the worktree `CodexBar.app/Contents/MacOS/CodexBar` remained running.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- Interactive widget click-through was not manually exercised; deterministic intent, snapshot, and app-group tests cover the paths.\n- Cursor estimates are explicitly local diagnostics and do not replace Cursor billing or request-based quota statements.\n\n## Plan\n\nThe implementation plan is marked completed in `docs/plans/2026-07-11-restore-cursor-widget-and-opencode-parity.md`.\n",
